@echo off
rem asight collector: launch shim for Kimi Code on Windows (RFC 4.8 s6.3), written by the user-path opt-in item of
rem `asight on kimi-code --opt-in kimi-code.cli`. It sets the CA file Node reads (the asight CA, plus any CA you
rem already gave Kimi Code) and this form's kernel listener; an HTTPS_PROXY the shell already set is your choice for
rem that run and is not overridden (that run is not captured). `asight off kimi-code` removes it.
if not defined HTTPS_PROXY set "HTTPS_PROXY=__ASIGHT_PROXY__"
set "NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=__ASIGHT_CA_FILE__"
"__ASIGHT_REAL_BINARY__" %*
